---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About CricBreakdown | Cricket Analysis, Insights & History" description="CricBreakdown is an independent cricket analysis and editorial platform covering match insights, player performances, pitch conditions, team strategies, IPL, cricket history and the stories behind the game." canonical="https://www.cricbreakdown.com/about">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pt-16 pb-24">
    <span class="stat-chip text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-leather">About CricBreakdown</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl md:text-5xl text-pitch mt-2 mb-8">
      Cricket analysis beyond the scorecard.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-pitch prose-a:text-leather">
      <p>
        <strong>CricBreakdown is an independent cricket analysis and editorial platform</strong>
        focused on explaining the performances, decisions, conditions and moments that shape the game.
        We cover international cricket, domestic cricket, the IPL and major tournaments, bringing together
        match analysis, player statistics, team strategy and cricket history in one place.
      </p>

      <h2>How we analyse the game</h2>
      <p>
        Our coverage looks beyond headlines and scorecards. We study relevant opinions and assessments
        from established cricket experts, then examine them alongside match data, player records,
        recent form, head-to-head matchups, team combinations and available pitch and playing-condition
        reports. This helps us assess the context behind a performance or selection decision rather
        than relying on a single opinion or statistic.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pitch behaviour, venue history, conditions and player strengths all matter. Where relevant,
        we connect these factors to explain why a team may choose a particular combination, how a
        batter or bowler could match up against an opponent, and what might influence the outcome.
        Analysis and predictions are presented as informed assessments, not as confirmed facts.
      </p>

      <h2>What CricBreakdown covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Match and series analysis:</strong> key turning points, performances, tactics and results.</li>
        <li><strong>Player performance:</strong> form, career records, statistical trends and important matchups.</li>
        <li><strong>Team strategy:</strong> squad selection, playing XIs, combinations, strengths and weaknesses.</li>
        <li><strong>IPL coverage:</strong> team-by-team analysis, auction strategy, player retentions and releases.</li>
        <li><strong>Cricket history and chronicles:</strong> memorable matches, milestones, rivalries, records and stories that shaped the sport.</li>
        <li><strong>Tournaments and series:</strong> coverage of international competitions, World Cups and domestic cricket.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our editorial approach</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to make every article clear, useful and grounded in context. Statistical claims are
        checked against available scorecards and reliable records; expert views are considered with
        attribution where used; and analysis is kept distinct from reported facts. When information
        changes or an error is identified, the relevant article should be reviewed and corrected.
        Our goal is not simply to repeat what happened, but to explain why it mattered.
      </p>

      <h2>Independent cricket coverage</h2>
      <p>
        CricBreakdown is an independent publication. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        officially connected to the BCCI, ICC, IPL or any cricket team or franchise mentioned on
        this website. Opinions and predictions are editorial analysis and do not represent official
        statements from players, teams or governing bodies.
      </p>

      <h2>Our purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Cricket has a story behind every score, selection, spell and turning point. CricBreakdown
        exists to document those stories and make the game easier to understand through thoughtful
        analysis, relevant statistics and historical context—for cricket fans who want more than
        just the final result.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
